---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StandaloneMatchmaker from '../components/StandaloneMatchmaker.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="What Can Your GPU Run? Local LLM Matchmaker"
  description="Pick your GPU memory, system RAM and context length to see which local LLMs fit fully on the GPU, need CPU offload or do not fit."
>
  <section class="max-w-shell mx-auto px-lg pt-2xl pb-md">
    <h1 class="text-display-hero text-primary max-w-reading">What can your GPU run?</h1>
    <p class="text-body-lg text-secondary max-w-reading mt-md">
      Set your GPU memory, system RAM and context length. The list sorts every synced
      model into Full GPU fit, Offload required or Out of memory, using the same formula as
      the VRAM calculator: (weights + KV cache) × 1.10.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-shell mx-auto px-lg pb-xl">
    <StandaloneMatchmaker />
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-shell mx-auto px-lg pb-2xl">
    <h2 class="text-headline-md text-primary">How these numbers are made</h2>
    <p class="text-body-md text-secondary max-w-reading mt-sm">
      Model file sizes come from the synced GGUF files. The KV cache is computed from each
      model's attention layout at the context length you pick, then 10% is added for runtime
      overhead. Everything is an estimate, not a measurement. See the
      <a href="/methodology" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline">methodology</a> for the full
      formula, or open the <a href="/hardware" class="text-accent-primary hover:underline">VRAM calculator</a>
      to check one model, an Apple Silicon Mac or several GPUs.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>